+# M10.5 · Matter-wave dispersion in paired Interval Echo material
+
+**Decision requested at registration.** Is the locally commissioned material and its collective detector admissible as a new state and decoder under the column's single-candidate rule? Under what scope would this observer test count for row 30? A cell decision requires a separate results review. The published simplest test asks for emergent matter-wave dispersion with a positive rest term. The M10 entry is untested and records that the earlier kinetic source installed the dispersion. The M5 precedent gives partial credit for six vacuum branches with a supplied time term. These comparisons inform the scope, without attaching another model's specific falsifier to M10. [Criterion](https://github.com/openwave-labs/openwave/blob/d4fc3e4046c472f4ad38468df8dddfa1f97bac97/MODELS.md#L136) · [M10](https://github.com/openwave-labs/openwave/blob/d4fc3e4046c472f4ad38468df8dddfa1f97bac97/MODELS.md#L467) · [M5](https://github.com/openwave-labs/openwave/blob/d4fc3e4046c472f4ad38468df8dddfa1f97bac97/MODELS.md#L198)
+
+The single adopted Interval Echo candidate is at RER commit `4fe10f9ac3e81423155fb3ac7baaf0fdb4c0b11c`. Its native local generator and all three federation fixtures are frozen below. The prior M10.3 row-4 pair detector, free-update rule and row-30 strand protocol are distinct. PR 749 proposes `09f062f77f7f540f2783f128ae6314c5d8b818ea` for the stability of two loads and eleven written memories. At the baseline this was an open proposal for row 4. It grants no row-30 status. An intervening candidate change requires new adjudication before acquisition. [Canonical specification](https://github.com/openwave-labs/openwave/blob/d4fc3e4046c472f4ad38468df8dddfa1f97bac97/openwave/xperiments/m10_oph/research/m10_theory_canonical.md#1-specification-of-record-and-the-pin) · [Pending row-4 proposal](https://github.com/openwave-labs/openwave/pull/749)
+
+**Frozen source manifest SHA-256 `3789a7be528ab9d20471486816df3f3ee39b003eb54c09eab3cd50d65629d4c9`.** The companion manifest identifies the source and local calibration bytes. Preserve this task's exact UTF-8 bytes, including its final LF. The proposed roadmap task M10.5 uses `openwave/xperiments/m10_oph/research/tasks/m10_5_task_details.md`. M10.4 belongs to the separate row-4 proposal.
+
+### Prior exposure and supplied material
+
+Development already tested seeds 312141, 312142 and 312143 on all three board sizes. An internal holdout using seed 927016 also passed the previously specified frequency, transport, zero-flight-contrast and square-root-versus-parabola gates. The shape comparisons and the ordinary-wave-number test below must therefore be read as confirmatory tests of a known candidate. Pilot coefficients and branches, the local Ising reduction, favorable and adverse prepared-guide results, failure of the earlier free blank load to yield the claimed massive scalar, and the previously selected contrast coupling κ=8 were known before this draft. κ=8 was explored in the earlier source sweep. Additional exploratory measurements enrolled two multicell rings among the twelve inspected matching patterns. Physical pair-line measurements reconstructed a zero-wave-number frequency near 15 on both, and near 7 at half flight contrast. The ring experiment uses the same local interactions and a different closed material preparation. Its results are disclosed as prior knowledge and have no role in selecting the prospective open strands. No particle species, dimensional energy scale or physically privileged choice of that coupling is predicted here.
+
+The preparer supplies loads, addresses, matched equal-degree dimers, conditional link memories, empty collars, allowed local pulses and a seeded event ordering. The whole-board matching rule supplies degree-at-most-two components. Enrollment uses the first longest open component in fixed traversal order, without choosing by its spectrum. Every board remains enrolled, including a short, single-cell, uninformative or failed preparation. An independent clock, Pauli measurements, spatial launch profiles and an upper-half positive-frequency search window are detector settings. Free native evolution determines the time records after release. The target is one collective orientation branch on a prepared strand. Relations along its one-dimensional dimer coordinate cannot establish isotropy on the whole federation. Absolute single-excitation rest detection and an independently measured causal crossover across directions remain separate questions.
+
+### First public registration and selection
+
+1. Use the first first-parent commit after OpenWave main baseline `d4fc3e4046c472f4ad38468df8dddfa1f97bac97` that contains these exact bytes at the stated path. Its predecessor must lack this version. Verify the committed blob, the frozen local source manifest, and the adopted candidate before deriving any settings. Publish the RER frozen sources before proposing these terms. At the same landing, add the companion file at the identical path with extension .source in place of .md. Its complete content is the 40 lowercase hexadecimal digits of that public RER release commit followed by one LF. Verify its ancestry on official RER main and compare the committed source files with the frozen manifest. An incomplete first landing remains invalid. Withdrawal or amendment of the task or its pointer bars acquisition under this version. A pull-request head, local commit, later restoration, merge prediction or amended text supplies no eligible anchor. There is one release and no reroll. A newly numbered/path-changed proposal requires a fresh published version.
+2. For each level 0, 1, 2, hash ASCII `OPH-OW30-collective-confirmation-v1:`, the first public registration SHA as 40 lowercase hex characters, a colon, and the level's decimal numeral. Interpret the first eight digest bytes unsigned big-endian and set the high bit. Each board selector has 63 variable digest bits. A collision between levels invalidates the draw. The reserved upper half of uint64 excludes every disclosed development and internal-validation seed. The official merge hash is a public reproducible selector. This is confirmation on fresh settings, with known mechanism and pilot results, and carries no cryptographic randomness or uniform-sampling claim.
+3. In the control arm retain every prepared collar and set the contrast coupling to zero during flight. Apply the same commissioning, timing, input profiles, paired branch reconstruction, zero-flight-contrast controls and terminal detectors to 20, 80 and 320 cells, respectively. Binomial aggregate counts simulate the exact distribution of the specified local readings. Record all returned and quiet counts. Save both clock hands, complete time and spatial count arrays for every stimulated mode pair, both remote source arms and controls, physical addresses, seed and preparation digest. The observer decoder extracts pair frequencies and spatial wave numbers from those records. Decomposition of three independent pair sums gives the first branch frequency. An unobserved single-particle line at zero wave number is not a datum.
+4. Read the preexisting disjoint meter counts. Their central estimates, with no bulk refitting, determine m = 2|J − h| and c² = 4Jh in clock and dimer-spacing units. Meter positivity requires J > h > 0. In addition, each control's absolute phase rate must be below 0.005. The estimated m = 15.00051 and c² = 16.00156 and their counting uncertainty were already known. The controlled coupling meter measures a spatial-gradient coefficient through the finite-chain reduction; it does not measure the packet's speed directly.
+5. On **every** board count all modes and all withheld pair sums. Require successful commissioning on the enrolled component with more than one physical cell. Require every frequency to agree within 0.0048 hand-frequency units with the local meter forecast √[m² + c²(2 − 2 cos k)], and every withheld pair sum closure error below 0.0048. The absolute test retains the intercept. On the ordinary spatial wave numbers 0 < k ≤ 0.50, in radians per dimer, require at least two enrolled wave numbers separated by 0.02 radians per dimer or more on each board and absolute errors below 0.0048 against √(m² + c²k²). Tabulate all larger ordinary-k residuals as well. Reporting the graph gradient in place of the measured Bloch wave number cannot pass the ordinary-k gate.
+6. Compare the independently normalized lattice square root with the matched tangent m + c²(2 − 2 cos k)/(2m). Subtract the first measured frequency and each forecast's own first value. On all remaining modes the RMS square-root error must be less than half the matched-tangent error, on every board. This extra shape gate tests whether existing sensitivity separates these models despite the finite band being narrow. A successful local long-wave fit alone does not settle line shape at larger wave number.
+7. Every stimulated pair's native sum-line amplitude must exceed 0.40. Its same-source zero-flight-contrast amplitude must be below 0.02, and that same control reader's amplitude at frequency 2 must exceed 0.40. At exposure 2, 4 or 8, at least one terminal address three or more strand bonds from both preparations, in a cell distinct from both, must have absolute source-minus-reference count fraction above 0.02. At every such distant address and exposure the zero-flight-contrast absolute count difference must be below 0.005.
+8. Each condition is evaluated at full machine precision. A failed gate retains its release and marks the confirmation rejected. A missing count, incomplete acquisition, changed pin, unverified bytes or failed replay is reported as incomplete or invalid. A later replay of the same draw may recover an interrupted file transfer. It cannot change seeds, gates, commissioning, enrollment or decoder. Require all integer readings to replay exactly with the frozen scientific Python versions and other numeric results to agree within 10⁻⁸ absolute. Cross-platform disagreement remains visible pending investigation. Maintainers adjudicate which effective description and cell, if any, the result supports.
+
+The OpenWave execution entry point is `openwave/xperiments/m10_oph/research/scripts/m10_5/run.py`. Its version, import layout and method are bound by the source manifest. After registration, execute the fixed implementation from an OpenWave checkout descending from the accepted registration. Publish the run receipts and request adjudication in the results submission.
+
+This text requests review of prospective terms. The internal holdout and known development results are not the future registered acquisition.
