+# Candidate request for a coherent dimer strand
+
+The authors request registration of a matter-wave dispersion experiment for row 30. The preparation places one load on each dimer of a commissioned strand. Independent local clocks, coupling measurements and two sets of receiver records compare the measured frequencies with independently measured wavelengths. The experiment nominates a new state, connecting memories and decoder on the Interval Echo law. Its frozen declaration and terms describe their historical comparison with M10.3. The current candidate is the M10.4 pair with eleven written contacts. Its row-4 finding belongs to that preparation. [M10.4 review](../findings/m10_4_maintainer_review.md) · [Frozen terms](../scripts/m10_5/vendor/model/candidate_laws/interval_echo/openwave/row_30_collective/confirmation/TASK.md)
+
+The authors have exposed three local cohorts. The v2 rejection and subsequent v3 results accompany this request. The frozen v3 source is `92370140edfbdb0ac2be647b2b8166d821e5f1a2`. The public selector depends on the first official landing of the final task and affirmative decision. M10.5 is the requested task identifier. Official task numbering, candidate admission and eventual grading are separate decisions for the maintainers. [Author observations](../findings/m10_5_author_validation.md) · [Proposed source](https://github.com/FloatingPragma/observer-patch-holography/tree/92370140edfbdb0ac2be647b2b8166d821e5f1a2/model/candidate_laws/interval_echo/openwave/row_30_collective/confirmation)
+
+The three public board selectors will be deterministic functions of the first qualifying official first-parent commit. A person preparing that commit can compute it locally and can vary its contents or metadata. The frozen terms therefore bind one accepted history and supply no independent future randomness. The authors have not drawn or previewed prospective public selectors for this packet. The landing party can disclose any preview or choice among possible commits. The official public replay derives the selectors through the authenticated platform launcher. A manifest supplied by the claimant alone cannot establish their origin.
